  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      I have always believed that who we are is shaped by a combination of factors – our upbringing, our experiences and the choices we make. My closest friend grew up in a very strict household, yet she turned out to be one of the most open-minded and independent people I know. She once told me that her identity was not defined by her background but by the decisions she made as an adult. It took her years to come to terms with who she really was. On the whole, I think identity is not something we are born with – it's something we gradually construct throughout our lives.
    </p>

    <h3>Osobowość i tożsamość – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">upbringing</td><td class="pl">wychowanie</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">identity</td><td class="pl">tożsamość</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">self-esteem</td><td class="pl">poczucie własnej wartości</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">self-image</td><td class="pl">obraz samego siebie</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">personality trait</td><td class="pl">cecha osobowości</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">attitude</td><td class="pl">postawa</td></tr>
