  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Family relationships are rarely simple. My parents divorced when I was ten, and for a long time I couldn't come to terms with it. It took me years to understand that their separation didn't mean the end of our family – it simply changed its shape. Today I have a good relationship with both of them, though it's complicated in different ways. I've also learned that you can't choose your relatives, but you can choose how much you let them affect you. Some relationships naturally drift apart; others become deeper over time. In the end, what matters is mutual respect and the willingness to work through problems rather than avoid them.
    </p>

    <h3>Relacje – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">relative</td><td class="pl">krewny</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">sibling</td><td class="pl">rodzeństwo</td></tr>
