    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Over the past few years, my eating habits have changed dramatically. I used to live on fast food and ready meals, but at some point I realised I wasn't doing myself any favours. I started cooking from scratch and cut down on processed food. I also try to eat more wholegrain products, fresh vegetables and fruit. Of course, I still have a sweet tooth and I sometimes treat myself to a piece of cake – I don't believe in strict diets. In my opinion, the key to a healthy lifestyle is balance rather than deprivation. As long as you eat sensibly most of the time, an occasional treat won't do you any harm.
