    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      The education system has changed a great deal over the past two decades. When my parents were at school, teachers relied heavily on lectures and memorisation. Nowadays the emphasis is on critical thinking and problem-solving. I'm currently in my final year of secondary school and I'm in the middle of applying to universities. The entrance requirements are quite demanding – I need high grades and a strong personal statement. I've been revising intensively for the past few months. It's stressful, but I know it will pay off. I'm planning to take a gap year before I start my degree, so I can gain some work experience and travel a bit. In my view, that's just as important as what you learn in a classroom.
