window.LESSON_DATA["T11B2"] = {
  tytul: "Komunikacja w pracy – poziom zaawansowany",
  poziom: "B2",
  dzial: "T11",
  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Effective communication is one of the most important skills in any workplace. In my company we use a mix of formal and informal channels – emails for clients, chat apps for quick internal messages, and video calls for meetings that require real discussion. When I write to a client, I always use a formal register, full sentences and polite phrases. When I message my team, I'm much more relaxed. The key to any conversation at work is clarity. If we're not clear about what we want, misunderstandings happen and projects can go wrong. I've also learned that giving and receiving feedback is an art. Constructive criticism, delivered respectfully, can help people grow; destructive criticism only makes things worse. In the end, it's better to ask a question than to assume something.
    </p>

    <h3>Komunikacja w pracy – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">register</td><td class="pl">rejestr językowy (formalny/nieformalny)</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">formal / informal communication</td><td class="pl">komunikacja formalna / nieformalna</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">clarity</td><td class="pl">jasność</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">misunderstanding</td><td class="pl">nieporozumienie</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">feedback</td><td class="pl">informacja zwrotna</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">constructive criticism</td><td class="pl">konstruktywna krytyka</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">destructive criticism</td><td class="pl">destrukcyjna krytyka</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">negotiate</td><td class="pl">negocjować</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">clarify</td><td class="pl">wyjaśniać</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">delegate tasks</td><td class="pl">delegować zadania</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">address an issue</td><td class="pl">zająć się kwestią</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">follow up on sth</td><td class="pl">podjąć temat, wrócić do sprawy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">touch base with sb</td><td class="pl">skontaktować się, wymienić informacje</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">keep sb in the loop</td><td class="pl">informować kogoś na bieżąco</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Formalny vs nieformalny język</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Formalnie</th><th>Nieformalnie</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I would like to...</td><td class="en">I want to...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Could you please...?</td><td class="en">Can you...?</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I am writing to inform you...</td><td class="en">Just letting you know...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I would appreciate it if...</td><td class="en">It would be great if...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Please find attached...</td><td class="en">Here's the file...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Yours sincerely,</td><td class="en">Best, / Cheers,</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I look forward to your reply.</td><td class="en">Let me know.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Pisanie emaili – zwroty</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">Dear Mr / Ms Smith,</td><td class="pl">Szanowny Panie / Pani,</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Dear Sir or Madam,</td><td class="pl">Szanowni Państwo,</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I am writing with regard to...</td><td class="pl">Piszę w sprawie...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Further to our conversation...</td><td class="pl">W nawiązaniu do naszej rozmowy...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I would be grateful if you could...</td><td class="pl">Byłbym wdzięczny, gdyby Pan mógł...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Please do not hesitate to contact me.</td><td class="pl">Proszę się ze mną kontaktować.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I apologise for the delay in replying.</td><td class="pl">Przepraszam za opóźnienie w odpowiedzi.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Thank you for your prompt reply.</td><td class="pl">Dziękuję za szybką odpowiedź.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Spotkania – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">agenda</td><td class="pl">porządek obrad</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">minutes</td><td class="pl">protokół</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">action points</td><td class="pl">zadania do wykonania</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">take the minutes</td><td class="pl">protokołować</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">chair a meeting</td><td class="pl">przewodniczyć spotkaniu</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">brainstorm ideas</td><td class="pl">burza mózgów</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">reach a consensus</td><td class="pl">osiągnąć konsensus</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">sum up</td><td class="pl">podsumować</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Wyrażanie opinii i zgody / niezgody</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">I see your point, but...</td><td class="pl">Rozumiem, o co ci chodzi, ale...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I couldn't agree more.</td><td class="pl">Zgadzam się w pełni.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I'm afraid I have to disagree.</td><td class="pl">Obawiam się, że muszę się nie zgodzić.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">With all due respect, ...</td><td class="pl">Przy całym szacunku, ...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Let's meet halfway.</td><td class="pl">Znajdźmy kompromis.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">That's a fair point.</td><td class="pl">To słuszna uwaga.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Could you clarify what you mean?</td><td class="pl">Czy możesz wyjaśnić, co masz na myśli?</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Let me get back to you on that.</td><td class="pl">Wrócę do tego tematu.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <b>Zapamiętaj:</b><br>
      <b>keep sb in the loop</b> = informować kogoś na bieżąco<br>
      <b>touch base with sb</b> = skontaktować się, wymienić informacje<br>
      W formalnym emailu: <b>Yours sincerely</b> (znasz nazwisko) vs <b>Yours faithfully</b> (Dear Sir/Madam)
    </div>
  `,
  karta: [
    { type: "header", text: "A. Uzupełnij zdanie słowem z tekstu" },
