    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Living in a democratic society means both enjoying rights and fulfilling responsibilities. Among our basic rights are freedom of speech, the right to vote and the right to a fair trial. At the same time, we have certain obligations – paying taxes, obeying the law and respecting the rights of others. Sometimes these two sides are in conflict. For example, freedom of speech doesn't mean we can say anything we want; we still have to respect other people and not spread hate speech or misinformation. A few months ago I had to make a formal complaint about a product I'd bought online. I learned how important it is to know your consumer rights and to be polite but firm when you complain. In the end, the company gave me a full refund.
    </p>

    <h3>Prawa i obowiązki – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">human rights</td><td class="pl">prawa człowieka</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">civil rights</td><td class="pl">prawa obywatelskie</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">freedom of speech</td><td class="pl">wolność słowa</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">right to vote</td><td class="pl">prawo do głosowania</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">fair trial</td><td class="pl">sprawiedliwy proces</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">citizen</td><td class="pl">obywatel</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">citizenship</td><td class="pl">obywatelstwo</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">democracy</td><td class="pl">demokracja</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">the rule of law</td><td class="pl">praworządność</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">obligation / duty</td><td class="pl">obowiązek</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">pay taxes</td><td class="pl">płacić podatki</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">obey the law</td><td class="pl">przestrzegać prawa</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">consumer rights</td><td class="pl">prawa konsumenta</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">refund / replacement</td><td class="pl">zwrot / wymiana</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Składanie reklamacji</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">make a complaint</td><td class="pl">złożyć reklamację</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">complain about sth</td><td class="pl">skarżyć się na coś</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">ask for a refund</td><td class="pl">poprosić o zwrot</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">ask for a replacement</td><td class="pl">poprosić o wymianę</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">the product was faulty</td><td class="pl">produkt był wadliwy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">it broke after a week</td><td class="pl">zepsuło się po tygodniu</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">it didn't match the description</td><td class="pl">nie zgadzał się z opisem</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I'm not satisfied with...</td><td class="pl">Nie jestem zadowolony z...</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Zwroty formalne – reklamacja</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">I would like to make a complaint about...</td><td class="pl">Chciałbym złożyć reklamację na...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I am writing to complain about...</td><td class="pl">Piszę, aby złożyć reklamację na...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I bought the product on (date).</td><td class="pl">Kupiłem produkt w dniu...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Unfortunately, it stopped working after...</td><td class="pl">Niestety, przestało działać po...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I would like a full refund / replacement.</td><td class="pl">Proszę o zwrot / wymianę.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I look forward to your reply.</td><td class="pl">Czekam na odpowiedź.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I have attached a copy of the receipt.</td><td class="pl">Załączam kopię paragonu.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Problemy społeczne i etyczne</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">discrimination</td><td class="pl">dyskryminacja</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">inequality</td><td class="pl">nierówność</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">hate speech</td><td class="pl">mowa nienawiści</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">censorship</td><td class="pl">cenzura</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">social justice</td><td class="pl">sprawiedliwość społeczna</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">activism</td><td class="pl">aktywizm</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">raise awareness</td><td class="pl">podnosić świadomość</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">take a stand</td><td class="pl">zająć stanowisko</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">stand up for one's rights</td><td class="pl">bronić swoich praw</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">turn a blind eye to sth</td><td class="pl">przymykać oko na coś</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Wyrażanie opinii o prawach</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">It is often argued that...</td><td class="pl">Często się argumentuje, że...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">From a legal point of view...</td><td class="pl">Z prawnego punktu widzenia...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">There is a fine line between...</td><td class="pl">Istnieje cienka granica między...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">This raises important questions about...</td><td class="pl">To rodzi ważne pytania o...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">We should not turn a blind eye to...</td><td class="pl">Nie powinniśmy przymykać oka na...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">It goes without saying that...</td><td class="pl">Jest oczywiste, że...</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <b>Zapamiętaj:</b><br>
      <b>make a complaint</b> · <b>complain about</b> · <b>ask for a refund</b><br>
      <b>stand up for one's rights</b> = bronić swoich praw<br>
      <b>turn a blind eye to sth</b> = przymykać oko na coś
    </div>
  `,
