  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      A few weeks ago I faced a difficult ethical decision. A colleague asked me to help him cover up a mistake he'd made at work – nothing dangerous, but something that could have serious consequences for the company. I felt torn between loyalty to a friend and my professional duty. On the one hand, I didn't want to get him into trouble; on the other hand, I knew that hiding the truth would only make things worse in the long run. In the end, I told him honestly that I couldn't help him cover it up, but that I would support him if he told our manager himself. He was angry at first, but a few days later he admitted I'd been right. Sometimes the hardest decisions are the ones that require us to be honest, even when honesty isn't popular.
    </p>

    <h3>Problemy i decyzje – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">dilemma</td><td class="pl">dylemat</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">ethical dilemma</td><td class="pl">dylemat etyczny</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">face a decision</td><td class="pl">stanąć przed decyzją</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">make a decision</td><td class="pl">podjąć decyzję</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">weigh up the pros and cons</td><td class="pl">rozważyć za i przeciw</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">be torn between</td><td class="pl">być rozdartym między</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">come to a conclusion</td><td class="pl">dojść do wniosku</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">in the long run</td><td class="pl">na dłuższą metę</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">take responsibility for</td><td class="pl">wziąć odpowiedzialność za</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">face the consequences</td><td class="pl">ponieść konsekwencje</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">do the right thing</td><td class="pl">zrobić właściwą rzecz</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">turn a blind eye to</td><td class="pl">przymykać oko na</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Etyka i wartości</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">honest / dishonest</td><td class="pl">uczciwy / nieuczciwy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">integrity</td><td class="pl">prawość, uczciwość</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">fair / unfair</td><td class="pl">sprawiedliwy / niesprawiedliwy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">loyalty</td><td class="pl">lojalność</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">conscience</td><td class="pl">sumienie</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">guilt</td><td class="pl">poczucie winy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">cover up</td><td class="pl">zataić, tuszować</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">admit a mistake</td><td class="pl">przyznać się do błędu</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">own up to sth</td><td class="pl">przyznać się do czegoś</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">take the blame</td><td class="pl">wziąć winę na siebie</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Wyrażanie wahań i opinii</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">I'm in two minds about it.</td><td class="pl">Nie jestem zdecydowany.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I have mixed feelings about it.</td><td class="pl">Mam mieszane uczucia.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I can see both sides of the argument.</td><td class="pl">Widzę argumenty obu stron.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">It's a tough call.</td><td class="pl">Trudna decyzja.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Whatever you do, ...</td><td class="pl">Cokolwiek zrobisz, ...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">It comes down to...</td><td class="pl">Sprowadza się to do...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">You have to draw the line somewhere.</td><td class="pl">Gdzieś trzeba postawić granicę.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Konstrukcje warunkowe – żal i hipoteza</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">If I had known, I would have acted differently.</td><td class="pl">Gdybym wiedział, postąpiłbym inaczej.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Had I listened to my instincts...</td><td class="pl">Gdybym posłuchał intuicji...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">I wish I hadn't done it.</td><td class="pl">Żałuję, że to zrobiłem.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">If only I could turn back time.</td><td class="pl">Gdybym tylko mógł cofnąć czas.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">It's no use crying over spilt milk.</td><td class="pl">Nie ma sensu płakać nad rozlanym mlekiem.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">What's done is done.</td><td class="pl">Co się stało, to się nie odstanie.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Reagowanie na problemy innych</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td class="en">I can see why you feel that way.</td><td class="pl">Rozumiem, dlaczego tak się czujesz.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Have you considered...?</td><td class="pl">Czy rozważałeś...?</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">If I were in your shoes, I would...</td><td class="pl">Na twoim miejscu...</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">It's not worth the risk.</td><td class="pl">Nie warto ryzykować.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">Whatever you decide, I'll support you.</td><td class="pl">Cokolwiek zdecydujesz, wesprę cię.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <b>Zapamiętaj:</b><br>
      <b>be torn between</b> = być rozdartym między<br>
      <b>turn a blind eye to</b> = przymykać oko na<br>
      <b>do the right thing</b> = zrobić właściwą rzecz<br>
      <b>It's no use crying over spilt milk</b> – idiomatyczne "nie ma sensu rozpaczać"
    </div>
  `,
