window.LESSON_DATA["T15B2"] = {
  tytul: "Ubrania, moda, wybory konsumenckie – poziom B2",
  poziom: "B2",
  dzial: "T15",
  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Fashion is about much more than just clothes – it's a way of expressing who we are and what we value. In recent years, there has been a growing interest in ethical and sustainable fashion. Many consumers are now far more conscious about where their clothes come from and how they were produced. Fast fashion, which offers cheap and trendy items, has been heavily criticised for its impact on the environment and on workers in developing countries. Instead of buying new clothes every month, many young people are choosing second-hand shops or swapping clothes with friends. Personally, I think it's a great trend. It saves money, it's better for the planet and it allows you to develop your own personal style. After all, true style has nothing to do with price tags.
    </p>

    <h3>Moda – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Angielski</th><th>Polski</th></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">fashion industry</td><td class="pl">przemysł modowy</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">trend / trendsetter</td><td class="pl">trend / kreator trendów</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">fast fashion</td><td class="pl">szybka moda</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">sustainable fashion</td><td class="pl">zrównoważona moda</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="en">ethical fashion</td><td class="pl">etyczna moda</td></tr>
