  dzial: "T16",
  teoria: `
    <h3>Tekst do zapamiętania</h3>
    <p class="en" style="display:block; padding:14px 18px; line-height:1.9;">
      Travelling is one of the best ways to broaden your horizons and learn about other cultures. Some people prefer organised package holidays, where everything is arranged for them – flights, hotels and transfers. Others swear by backpacking, which is cheaper and gives you much more freedom. I've tried both, and personally I enjoy backpacking more. Last year I spent three weeks travelling around Portugal with two friends. We stayed in hostels, used public transport and ate in small local restaurants. We didn't plan everything in advance – sometimes we just arrived in a new city and decided what to do next. Of course, not everything went smoothly. Once we missed a train and had to wait five hours at a small station in the middle of nowhere. But looking back, those unexpected moments were exactly what made the trip memorable. I think everyone should travel abroad at least once in their life.
    </p>

    <h3>Podróże – słownictwo B2</h3>
    <table>
